Description: Build against FUSE 3
 Debian forky no longer ships libfuse-dev (FUSE 2). Ceph's CMake already
 prefers fuse3 when it is available, so only the build dependency changes.
 The runtime dependency on "fuse" is satisfied by fuse3 on forky.
---
--- a/debian/control
+++ b/debian/control
@@ -42,7 +42,7 @@
                libexpat1-dev,
                libffi-dev [!amd64] <pkg.ceph.check>,
                libfmt-dev (>= 6.1.2),
-               libfuse-dev,
+               libfuse3-dev,
                libgoogle-perftools-dev [i386 amd64 arm64],
                libgnutls28-dev <pkg.ceph.crimson>,
                libhwloc-dev <pkg.ceph.crimson>,
